### What happened?

When the docs are served by Laravel Octane, only the **first** request to a worker returns the complete OpenAPI document. Every later request handled by the same worker is missing the inferred query parameters, e.g. `page` / `per_page` from `->paginate($request->integer('per_page', 15))`, `search`, and `$request->input(...)` filters.

In our API the parameter count drops from 445 to 311 (53 of 370 operations are affected). `php artisan scramble:export` is not affected because it generates only once per process.

| version | params on requests 1 / 2 / 3 (one Octane worker) |
|---|---|
| 0.13.45 | 445 / 445 / 445 |
| 0.13.46 – 0.13.49 | 445 / **311** / **311** |

**Bisected to 75bb944 "Model accessors" (#1278)**, which added this to `ScrambleServiceProvider::boot()`:

    Scramble::infer()->configure()->buildDefinitionsUsingAstFor([Attribute::class]);

`Scramble::infer()` resolves the `Infer` singleton, and with it the `Index` singleton, at boot. Octane boots once and runs every request in a clone of the booted app, so singletons resolved at boot are shared by all requests in a worker. The second generation then runs against a warm `Index` and loses the inferred request parameters. Before 0.13.46, `Index` was first resolved inside the request sandbox, so every request got a fresh one.

Removing only that boot block brings 0.13.46 and 0.13.49 back to 445 / 445 / 445.

The underlying issue is older: generating twice in the **same** container loses the parameters with 0.13.45 too, so generation isn't idempotent with a reused `Index`. #1278 only makes that visible under Octane.

