> **Correction (edited after filing):** my first version of this report blamed the custom builder subclass. That was wrong. The trigger is overriding `query()` on the **model**. A model that only overrides `newEloquentBuilder()` infers the whole chain correctly. The repro below has been rewritten accordingly.

### What happened?

Overriding `public static function query()` on a model, which is the usual way to advertise a custom Eloquent builder to an IDE and to static analysis, silently degrades the inferred builder type to `Builder<Model>`. Any subsequent call to a method that exists only on the custom builder (or a scope on the model) then resolves to nothing, and the field is documented as `{"type": "string"}`.

Two models, identical apart from the `query()` override, in one response:

```json
{
  "no_query_override_direct":   { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
  "no_query_override_custom":   { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
  "with_query_override_direct": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
  "with_query_override_custom": { "type": "string" }
}
```

from

```php
'no_query_override_direct'   => Widget2::query()->count(),
'no_query_override_custom'   => Widget2::query()->active()->count(),
'with_query_override_direct' => Widget::query()->count(),
'with_query_override_custom' => Widget::query()->active()->count(),
```

`Widget2` overrides only `newEloquentBuilder()`. `Widget` overrides `newEloquentBuilder()` **and** `query()`. Everything about the builder subclass is otherwise the same, and subclass forwarding evidently works fine, since `Widget2` infers correctly.

Note that `count()` still infers on the degraded type, because it comes from `Builder`'s `@mixin \Illuminate\Database\Query\Builder`. Only the custom method is lost, and losing it takes the rest of the chain with it.

It is not caused by the declared return type. `static`, `self` and the explicit class name behave the same, and so does a method whose body is just `return $this;`. Adding `@mixin \Illuminate\Database\Query\Builder` to the builder subclass changes nothing.

### How to reproduce the bug

`app/Builders/WidgetBuilder.php`

```php
<?php

namespace App\Builders;

use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Builder;

/**
 * @template TModel of \Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model
 *
 * @extends Builder<TModel>
 */
class WidgetBuilder extends Builder
{
    public function active(): static
    {
        return $this->where('active', true);
    }
}
```

`app/Models/Widget.php` — with the override, broken

```php
<?php

namespace App\Models;

use App\Builders\WidgetBuilder;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;

class Widget extends Model
{
    /** @return WidgetBuilder<static> */
    public static function query(): WidgetBuilder
    {
        return parent::query();
    }

    /** @return WidgetBuilder<static> */
    public function newEloquentBuilder($query): WidgetBuilder
    {
        return new WidgetBuilder($query);
    }
}
```

`app/Models/Widget2.php` — without the override, works

```php
<?php

namespace App\Models;

use App\Builders\WidgetBuilder;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;

class Widget2 extends Model
{
    /** @return WidgetBuilder<static> */
    public function newEloquentBuilder($query): WidgetBuilder
    {
        return new WidgetBuilder($query);
    }
}
```

`routes/api.php`

```php
Route::get('/widget-stats', fn () => response()->json([
    'no_query_override_direct' => Widget2::query()->count(),
    'no_query_override_custom' => Widget2::query()->active()->count(),
    'with_query_override_direct' => Widget::query()->count(),
    'with_query_override_custom' => Widget::query()->active()->count(),
]));
```

Run `php artisan scramble:export` and read the 200 response schema for `/widget-stats`.

