### Notes

Reproduced on a fresh `laravel/laravel` install with only `dedoc/scramble` added, no other configuration.

I did not verify the following, so treat it as a lead rather than a diagnosis. `AfterModelDefinitionCreatedExtension` appears to seed a synthetic `query` definition that produces the correct builder type, which would explain why `Widget2` works. When the model declares its own `query()`, `ClassDefinition::lazilyLoadMethodDefinition` finds a reflection method whose declaring class is the model itself and replaces the seeded definition with one analysed from the AST. Analysing `return parent::query()` then resolves against the base `Model`'s seeded definition, which is built from `Model` rather than from late static binding, so the result is `Builder<Model>`. The declared `: WidgetBuilder` return type does not override the inferred one.

Workaround for anyone hitting this: drop the `query()` override and keep only `newEloquentBuilder()`. That costs the IDE hint the override was there to provide.
